   "subject": "Re: How to highlight the edges of a polygon",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Viviana,<div><br></div><div>This isn&#39;t strictly about the R package geomorph, this is about using the R package rgl. But rgl.material is probably where you need to experiment.</div><div><br></div><div>Plot the mesh using mesh3d() and play with the settings of rgl.material, particularly <div>  ambient      </div><div>  specular    </div><div>  emission  </div><div><br></div><div>You can also overlay the triangles using lines3d() in a different colour entirely if you wish.</div><div><br></div><div>Emma   </div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Thursday, 31 August 2017 00:29:01 UTC+9:30, Viviana Toro-Ibacache  wrote:</div></div>"
    ],
